1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,000


2
00:00:28,670 --> 00:00:29,900
Your lease isn't up yet.

3
00:00:30,190 --> 00:00:31,420
And you two, living one above the other,

4
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:32,980
are both moving out?

5
00:00:33,920 --> 00:00:34,950
This is so sudden.

6
00:00:34,950 --> 00:00:36,180
How am I supposed to find

7
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:37,690
new tenants on such short notice?

8
00:00:37,920 --> 00:00:38,500
Right?

9
00:00:38,750 --> 00:00:39,620
It's okay.

10
00:00:40,240 --> 00:00:41,540
You can keep the deposit.

11
00:00:41,880 --> 00:00:43,580
Consider it compensation.

12
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,860
So you're moving out together?

13
00:00:48,640 --> 00:00:50,180
If I'd known you two knew each other,

14
00:00:50,200 --> 00:00:52,410
I'd have offered you my bigger apartment.

15
00:00:52,430 --> 00:00:53,770
Want to take a look?

16
00:00:53,790 --> 00:00:54,650
No, thanks.

17
00:00:56,190 --> 00:00:56,720
Alright.

18
00:01:01,240 --> 00:01:03,380
Do you still want this?

19
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:04,580
Yes, I'll keep it.

20
00:01:06,500 --> 00:01:07,300
Okay, then.

21
00:01:07,930 --> 00:01:09,290
Well, I'll get going.

22
00:01:09,310 --> 00:01:10,490
Okay. Thank you.

23
00:02:16,080 --> 00:02:16,850
Hello?

24
00:02:30,910 --> 00:02:31,690
Hello?

25
00:02:46,190 --> 00:02:47,170
Jiang Ming.

26
00:02:56,910 --> 00:02:57,890
Where are you?

27
00:03:55,580 --> 00:03:57,020
♪I remember how my fingertips♪

28
00:03:57,180 --> 00:04:00,020
♪Once lingered on your face♪

29
00:04:01,660 --> 00:04:02,900
♪It feels so far away♪

30
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:04,380
♪Yet my memories of you♪

31
00:04:04,580 --> 00:04:07,140
♪Seem frozen in the past♪

32
00:04:08,700 --> 00:04:10,500
♪We never said goodbye♪

33
00:04:10,700 --> 00:04:12,420
♪We parted without a word in the end♪

34
00:04:12,580 --> 00:04:16,500
♪Silently, we drifted apart♪

35
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:18,060
♪I don't blame you♪

36
00:04:18,180 --> 00:04:19,660
♪I'll tell myself I once had♪

37
00:04:19,740 --> 00:04:23,140
♪I'll tell myself I once had you♪

38
00:04:25,540 --> 00:04:27,380
♪I wanted us to share♪

39
00:04:27,420 --> 00:04:29,700
♪A simple life without regrets♪

40
00:04:31,780 --> 00:04:33,140
♪And I almost told you♪

41
00:04:33,340 --> 00:04:34,460
♪What that rush of tears♪

42
00:04:34,540 --> 00:04:37,900
♪Had moved me to promise♪

43
00:04:38,860 --> 00:04:40,540
♪It's a shame that you and I♪

44
00:04:40,660 --> 00:04:42,180
♪Were bound to face a rough road♪

45
00:04:42,340 --> 00:04:44,700
♪Bound to go nowhere♪

46
00:04:45,260 --> 00:04:47,540
♪I won't be sad♪

47
00:04:48,260 --> 00:04:49,620
♪I'll tell myself I once had♪

48
00:04:49,780 --> 00:04:53,340
♪I'll tell myself I once had you♪

49
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:56,780
♪I won't cry...♪

50
00:05:01,830 --> 00:05:02,850
You like jellyfish?

51
00:05:05,040 --> 00:05:06,020
I do.

52
00:05:07,160 --> 00:05:08,370
Ever since I was little.

53
00:05:10,510 --> 00:05:12,020
Jellyfish don't live very long.

54
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:13,980
When they die,

55
00:05:14,830 --> 00:05:16,100
they dissolve into the water.

56
00:05:17,360 --> 00:05:18,580
It's like they just disappear.

57
00:05:20,190 --> 00:05:21,140
Without a trace.

58
00:05:22,240 --> 00:05:23,250
Nothing left behind.

59
00:05:25,660 --> 00:05:27,220
♪I've already etched you into my memory♪

60
00:05:27,340 --> 00:05:30,340
♪I hope you won't forget me either♪

61
00:05:31,620 --> 00:05:32,940
♪You did nothing wrong♪

62
00:05:33,140 --> 00:05:34,460
♪I was the one who overdid it♪

63
00:05:34,580 --> 00:05:38,220
♪My feelings only brought you pain♪

64
00:05:38,660 --> 00:05:40,420
♪At least I can♪

65
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:42,180
♪Untouched by partings, reunions, joy or sorrow♪

66
00:05:42,340 --> 00:05:44,740
♪And simply be grateful that I met you♪

67
00:05:44,980 --> 00:05:46,300
♪That's all♪

68
00:05:48,260 --> 00:05:49,620
♪I'll tell myself I once had♪

69
00:05:49,780 --> 00:05:53,500
♪I'll tell myself I once had you♪

70
00:05:53,820 --> 00:05:56,340
♪I won't cry♪

71
00:07:46,060 --> 00:07:47,500
[The Story Untold]

72
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:50,140
[Based on Twentine's novel "The Story Untold" on jjwxc.net]

73
00:07:50,460 --> 00:07:53,340
[Episode 6]

74
00:07:53,540 --> 00:08:01,740
[Three Years Later, Qingcheng, 2013]

75
00:08:01,950 --> 00:08:03,540
Kintsukuroi uses raw lacquer

76
00:08:03,540 --> 00:08:05,290
as both an adhesive and a molding agent

77
00:08:05,830 --> 00:08:07,980
to put broken pottery back together.

78
00:08:08,870 --> 00:08:10,850
Finally, the repaired areas

79
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:12,540
[Kintsukuroi: Golden Repair - The Beauty of Imperfection]
are decorated with gold leaf.

80
00:08:12,920 --> 00:08:15,170
Today, we've invited a senior artifact conservator

81
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:16,340
who also serves as

82
00:08:16,360 --> 00:08:18,050
an art advisor at Qingcheng Normal University,

83
00:08:18,430 --> 00:08:19,250
Ms. Yang Zhao.

84
00:08:19,800 --> 00:08:21,490
She's brought six Jian tea bowls

85
00:08:21,950 --> 00:08:23,290
to demonstrate

86
00:08:23,310 --> 00:08:25,340
the different stages of kintsukuroi restoration.

87
00:08:26,950 --> 00:08:27,610
First,

88
00:08:28,040 --> 00:08:31,490
mix raw lacquer, flour, and water thoroughly.

89
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:33,610
The resulting adhesive

90
00:08:33,630 --> 00:08:35,300
is called wheat lacquer.

91
00:08:36,150 --> 00:08:39,100
Apply it evenly to the broken edges.

92
00:08:39,510 --> 00:08:41,610
This bonds the pieces back together.

93
00:08:43,510 --> 00:08:45,100
Some pottery has more extensive damage.

94
00:08:45,550 --> 00:08:47,490
The missing sections

95
00:08:47,510 --> 00:08:48,940
need new structural support.

96
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:50,940
This step is called reinforcement.

97
00:08:51,240 --> 00:08:52,850
Ms. Yang is now demonstrating

98
00:08:52,870 --> 00:08:55,420
how to build a framework using reinforcement.

99
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:58,420
Once all the damaged areas are reshaped

100
00:08:58,870 --> 00:09:00,650
and the lacquer base is firm and smooth,

101
00:09:01,150 --> 00:09:04,370
now comes the crucial step of applying the gold.

102
00:09:05,480 --> 00:09:06,610
In ancient times,

103
00:09:06,630 --> 00:09:09,220
there were three gilding methods: leaf, powder, and paste.

104
00:09:10,030 --> 00:09:11,460
Ms. Yang is now demonstrating

105
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:13,890
the most commonly used method: gold powder application.

106
00:09:14,750 --> 00:09:16,130
Once the gold has been applied,

107
00:09:16,150 --> 00:09:18,580
dab a silk ball in some gold powder

108
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:19,650
and gently brush it on.

109
00:09:19,910 --> 00:09:21,060
Keep buffing the surface

110
00:09:21,080 --> 00:09:22,820
until the gold takes on a richer shine.

111
00:09:23,870 --> 00:09:26,580
And that completes the kintsukuroi restoration process.

112
00:09:27,320 --> 00:09:28,130
Thank you, Ms. Yang,

113
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:30,220
for that wonderful demonstration.

114
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:34,610
Ms. Yang,

115
00:09:35,150 --> 00:09:37,820
antique restoration usually aims to preserve the original look.

116
00:09:37,840 --> 00:09:39,420
The top priority is often

117
00:09:39,440 --> 00:09:40,580
to make repairs invisible.

118
00:09:40,790 --> 00:09:43,770
But kintsukuroi takes the exact opposite approach.

119
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:45,490
What are your thoughts on that?

120
00:09:47,080 --> 00:09:48,370
Kintsukuroi restoration

121
00:09:48,390 --> 00:09:50,100
uses the most precious metal

122
00:09:50,120 --> 00:09:51,890
to highlight what's missing.

123
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:53,980
The goal isn't to hide the damage.

124
00:09:54,630 --> 00:09:55,460
In fact,

125
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:58,420
kintsukuroi gives an object a second life.

126
00:09:59,360 --> 00:10:01,260
Instead of hiding its flaws,

127
00:10:01,750 --> 00:10:02,890
we learn to accept them

128
00:10:03,480 --> 00:10:05,220
and find beauty in them.

129
00:10:06,200 --> 00:10:08,730
What kintsukuroi creates

130
00:10:08,750 --> 00:10:10,700
is a new kind of beauty from brokenness.

131
00:10:11,200 --> 00:10:12,610
In that sense,

132
00:10:13,150 --> 00:10:14,290
it's more than just restoration.

133
00:10:15,360 --> 00:10:16,580
It reminds us

134
00:10:17,270 --> 00:10:18,850
that life is full of unexpected changes

135
00:10:20,150 --> 00:10:21,220
and painful moments.

136
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:23,370
They're all part of its story.

137
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:26,180
And through kintsukuroi,

138
00:10:26,720 --> 00:10:28,370
all those broken pieces can come together

139
00:10:28,910 --> 00:10:30,420
and become something worth looking forward to.

140
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,490
Perhaps

141
00:10:34,200 --> 00:10:36,730
in a beautiful new form.

142
00:10:56,700 --> 00:10:59,000
[Beloved Father Yang Jianguo, Mother Zhang Xiuying]

143
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:00,530
Their devoted son, Yang Jintian?

144
00:11:00,530 --> 00:11:02,550
[Erected by Their Devoted Son, Yang Jintian]

145
00:11:02,550 --> 00:11:03,220
My younger brother.

146
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,830
Adopted or not, you're still their daughter.

147
00:11:09,700 --> 00:11:11,180
You even paid for their grave.

148
00:11:11,200 --> 00:11:12,890
And he couldn't even put your name on it?

149
00:11:15,510 --> 00:11:16,490
Where's this devoted son now?

150
00:11:21,670 --> 00:11:22,980
Mom and Dad died so suddenly.

151
00:11:23,670 --> 00:11:24,730
He took it pretty hard.

152
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:26,130
He's staying with relatives now.

153
00:11:28,600 --> 00:11:30,300
How does he treat you?

154
00:11:32,600 --> 00:11:35,130
I barely came home after going abroad to study.

155
00:11:36,670 --> 00:11:37,610
He resents me for that.

156
00:11:38,600 --> 00:11:39,980
If he doesn't appreciate what you're doing,

157
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,610
you shouldn't have to sacrifice so much

158
00:11:42,200 --> 00:11:43,530
just to stay in Qingcheng for him.

159
00:11:44,870 --> 00:11:45,530
Zhao.

160
00:11:48,550 --> 00:11:49,850
After the way your family's treated you,

161
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,270
you've done more than enough for them.

162
00:11:57,510 --> 00:11:58,530
Just think about it.

163
00:11:59,270 --> 00:12:00,100
Okay?

164
00:12:01,200 --> 00:12:02,530
Come back to California with me.

165
00:12:02,910 --> 00:12:04,490
We can move your studio back there.

166
00:12:05,150 --> 00:12:06,650
The Gold Coast.

167
00:12:06,790 --> 00:12:08,300
It's sunny all year round.

168
00:12:09,550 --> 00:12:10,650
We could live comfortably.

169
00:12:11,030 --> 00:12:11,940
Doesn't that sound nice?

170
00:12:13,840 --> 00:12:15,340
My brother takes his college entrance exams next year.

171
00:12:15,960 --> 00:12:18,370
I need to stay until he's finished them.

172
00:12:25,580 --> 00:12:27,580
[Yang Zhao: Yang Jintian,]

173
00:12:27,580 --> 00:12:35,060
[I sent this month's living expenses to Auntie. Call me back.]

174
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:38,420
Lucky!

175
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:40,300
Shoo! Shoo! Go on!

176
00:12:40,320 --> 00:12:40,980
Not here.

177
00:13:19,620 --> 00:13:40,500
[Please end my lease for me. Thanks. Jiang Ming]

178
00:13:50,030 --> 00:13:51,220
Don't drag that.

179
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:52,130
We'll need it again later.

180
00:13:52,150 --> 00:13:53,010
So what?

181
00:13:53,030 --> 00:13:53,980
We're not even allowed to touch it?

182
00:13:54,390 --> 00:13:56,060
Who knows where they found this big shot?

183
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:58,010
She gets her own assistant,

184
00:13:58,030 --> 00:13:59,530
her own lectures,

185
00:13:59,790 --> 00:14:00,700
and the whole VIP treatment.

186
00:14:01,320 --> 00:14:02,420
I heard

187
00:14:02,440 --> 00:14:04,300
she studied abroad

188
00:14:04,320 --> 00:14:05,770
and is a senior artifact conservator.

189
00:14:06,080 --> 00:14:07,580
She's an art advisor at our museum

190
00:14:07,670 --> 00:14:10,180
and teaches electives at the university.

191
00:14:10,870 --> 00:14:12,180
She looks younger than me.

192
00:14:12,550 --> 00:14:13,730
Aren't our advisors and professors

193
00:14:13,750 --> 00:14:15,820
usually old men with gray hair?

194
00:14:16,030 --> 00:14:17,340
Since when are advisors this young?

195
00:14:17,720 --> 00:14:18,980
Enough gossiping.

196
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,730
A while back,

197
00:14:20,870 --> 00:14:22,820
a friend of the director's, Mr. Xue,

198
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:24,650
donated some antiques to the museum.

199
00:14:24,960 --> 00:14:27,060
Then he insisted we hire a specific advisor.

200
00:14:27,080 --> 00:14:27,530
And now,

201
00:14:28,510 --> 00:14:29,250
here she is.

202
00:14:29,250 --> 00:14:30,510
[Kintsukuroi: Golden Repair - The Beauty of Imperfection]

203
00:14:30,510 --> 00:14:32,300
So she's not a real artifact conservator?

204
00:14:32,840 --> 00:14:33,940
She got the job through connections?

205
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:34,850
That explains it.

206
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:37,580
They're already giving her personal studio a full promotional tour.

207
00:14:38,150 --> 00:14:39,060
Isn't that a bit much?

208
00:14:39,080 --> 00:14:40,100
The more strings they pull,

209
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:41,650
the harder they have to sell it.

210
00:14:41,670 --> 00:14:43,180
Gotta make everything look good, right?

211
00:14:43,550 --> 00:14:44,850
Don't talk about Ms. Yang like that.

212
00:14:45,720 --> 00:14:48,580
Isn't Ms. Yang teaching students right now?

213
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:49,490
Maybe sometime

214
00:14:49,510 --> 00:14:50,820
we could sit in on one of her classes.

215
00:14:51,510 --> 00:14:52,130
Of course.

216
00:14:52,750 --> 00:14:54,650
You're welcome to sit in anytime.

217
00:14:54,910 --> 00:14:55,940
Thank you, Ms. Yang.

218
00:14:58,270 --> 00:14:59,010
Could you please

219
00:14:59,390 --> 00:15:01,180
take this late Qing Dynasty lapis lazuli court necklace

220
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:02,220
to my office?

221
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:02,890
This one?

222
00:15:02,910 --> 00:15:03,250
Yes.

223
00:15:04,270 --> 00:15:04,770
Okay.

224
00:15:08,600 --> 00:15:10,060
There's something you've got wrong.

225
00:15:10,750 --> 00:15:12,220
I didn't ask to come here.

226
00:15:12,510 --> 00:15:15,180
Your university hired me to restore this artifact.

227
00:15:15,870 --> 00:15:18,530
Once restored, it'll go to auction this fall.

228
00:15:18,910 --> 00:15:20,340
And the proceeds

229
00:15:20,630 --> 00:15:22,220
will be donated to the museum by Mr. Xue.

230
00:15:22,630 --> 00:15:23,730
I assume that's also

231
00:15:23,750 --> 00:15:26,010
how you're funding the museum's renovation.

232
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:27,130
Yes, that's right.

233
00:15:40,030 --> 00:15:40,710
Zhao.

234
00:15:43,270 --> 00:15:45,010
Why do you look extra gorgeous today?

235
00:15:45,620 --> 00:15:47,220
Did you change your lipstick shade?

236
00:15:47,630 --> 00:15:48,490
I haven't seen this one before.

237
00:15:49,320 --> 00:15:50,100
I booked a private dining room.

238
00:15:50,120 --> 00:15:51,490
Let's have dinner together tonight.

239
00:15:51,510 --> 00:15:53,300
You can get to know your coworkers.

240
00:15:53,840 --> 00:15:54,490
No, thanks.

241
00:15:56,440 --> 00:15:57,220
Then I'll cancel the reservation.

242
00:16:05,960 --> 00:16:06,850
Why are you wiping it off?

243
00:16:07,270 --> 00:16:08,490
That lipstick looks great on you.

244
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:11,580
I bought it just to restore the bowl you brought me.

245
00:16:12,790 --> 00:16:14,530
I couldn't mix the right paint color,

246
00:16:15,150 --> 00:16:16,940
so I tried different lipstick shades.

247
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:19,010
Stop wiping it off.

248
00:16:19,550 --> 00:16:20,580
I think it looks beautiful.

249
00:16:26,240 --> 00:16:27,130
By the way, how's that bowl coming along?

250
00:16:27,320 --> 00:16:28,100
How's the restoration?

251
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:29,100
Almost done?

252
00:16:30,750 --> 00:16:33,060
Restoration takes patience.

253
00:16:34,550 --> 00:16:36,770
I haven't even figured out how to fix it yet.

254
00:16:36,910 --> 00:16:37,580
Your time

255
00:16:37,600 --> 00:16:39,460
is too valuable to waste on something so minor.

256
00:16:39,720 --> 00:16:40,820
Just do a decent job.

257
00:16:45,270 --> 00:16:46,700
What's that look for?

258
00:16:47,600 --> 00:16:49,300
Okay, I know what you're going to say.

259
00:16:49,320 --> 00:16:49,980
That bowl

260
00:16:50,000 --> 00:16:52,130
was my grandma's treasured possession for decades.

261
00:16:52,320 --> 00:16:54,250
But it's really not worth much.

262
00:16:56,750 --> 00:16:57,980
That bowl holds

263
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,530
a lifetime of memories for your grandma.

264
00:17:01,030 --> 00:17:02,340
That makes it priceless.

265
00:17:17,400 --> 00:17:18,250
Lucky.

266
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,290
You've gotten heavy again.

267
00:17:22,960 --> 00:17:23,530
You know,

268
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:24,460
we went to school together.

269
00:17:24,750 --> 00:17:26,940
I even copied your homework in high school.

270
00:17:27,270 --> 00:17:29,250
How did our lives turn out so differently?

271
00:17:29,350 --> 00:17:30,660
You've got Mr. Xue.

272
00:17:31,240 --> 00:17:33,200
And all I've got

273
00:17:33,400 --> 00:17:34,570
are these cats and dogs.

274
00:17:34,830 --> 00:17:35,940
Don't be ridiculous.

275
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:37,700
Xue Miao is just my boss.

276
00:17:38,110 --> 00:17:39,770
What boss goes that far for an employee?

277
00:17:40,590 --> 00:17:42,460
He paid for you to study in Russia,

278
00:17:42,550 --> 00:17:44,180
took you around the world restoring artifacts,

279
00:17:44,340 --> 00:17:46,870
and donated an entire museum when you came back to Qingcheng.

280
00:17:47,750 --> 00:17:48,420
Hold on.

281
00:17:48,880 --> 00:17:49,770
Let me correct you.

282
00:17:50,440 --> 00:17:51,140
First,

283
00:17:51,510 --> 00:17:53,380
he didn't donate a museum.

284
00:17:53,960 --> 00:17:55,090
He's just trying to break into

285
00:17:55,110 --> 00:17:56,770
the domestic auction market.

286
00:17:57,400 --> 00:17:58,010
Second,

287
00:17:58,590 --> 00:18:00,570
he came to Qingcheng to oversee the work.

288
00:18:04,440 --> 00:18:05,090
Yang Zhao.

289
00:18:05,790 --> 00:18:07,140
You've been back for ages.

290
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:08,250
Stop shutting yourself off.

291
00:18:08,790 --> 00:18:10,290
When it comes to love,

292
00:18:10,510 --> 00:18:11,810
sometimes you just have to go with the flow.

293
00:18:13,030 --> 00:18:14,660
That's exactly what I can't stand.

294
00:18:15,200 --> 00:18:15,900
What is?

295
00:18:16,680 --> 00:18:18,010
Going with the flow.

296
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:20,700
Isn't that how you end up

297
00:18:20,960 --> 00:18:22,250
losing yourself along the way?

298
00:18:23,880 --> 00:18:25,980
How is that losing yourself?

299
00:18:26,790 --> 00:18:29,980
A funny, handsome, wealthy man...

300
00:18:30,070 --> 00:18:32,050
He's every woman's dream.

301
00:18:33,030 --> 00:18:34,330
But not mine.

302
00:18:35,960 --> 00:18:37,620
Okay, okay.

303
00:18:37,640 --> 00:18:39,660
You don't want what's handed to you.

304
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:40,860
You'd rather chase after someone.

305
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:43,290
That's just like you.

306
00:18:44,640 --> 00:18:45,330
Lucky.

307
00:18:45,350 --> 00:18:46,900
You're up.

308
00:18:47,440 --> 00:18:48,730
Okay, okay. Come on out.

309
00:18:50,070 --> 00:18:50,330
Come here.

310
00:18:52,240 --> 00:18:52,770
Hello?

311
00:18:53,960 --> 00:18:54,380
Hello.

312
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:56,980
Are you Yang Jintian's sister?

313
00:18:57,680 --> 00:18:58,330
Yes.

314
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:00,490
This is Lingkong Police Station.

315
00:19:00,920 --> 00:19:01,940
Your brother's here at the station.

316
00:19:01,960 --> 00:19:02,900
Please come down.

317
00:19:05,030 --> 00:19:06,730
Kids these days are hotheaded.

318
00:19:06,880 --> 00:19:07,620
One little disagreement,

319
00:19:07,640 --> 00:19:09,250
and they're fighting with a cab driver.

320
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:10,490
You're responsible for him.

321
00:19:10,830 --> 00:19:12,860
You ought to teach him how to behave.

322
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:13,770
Wake up.

323
00:19:15,920 --> 00:19:17,050
Look how drunk he is.

324
00:19:24,400 --> 00:19:25,220
Officer,

325
00:19:26,030 --> 00:19:26,980
where's the man who hit him?

326
00:19:27,550 --> 00:19:29,570
You ended up picking a fight with a woman in her eighties.

327
00:19:29,880 --> 00:19:30,690
What kind of person does that?

328
00:19:31,110 --> 00:19:32,700
Scum, that's who.

329
00:19:33,310 --> 00:19:34,270
Who are you calling scum?

330
00:19:34,270 --> 00:19:34,750
Sit down!

331
00:19:34,750 --> 00:19:35,620
- Who are you calling scum? - Sit down!

332
00:19:35,640 --> 00:19:36,700
- Who's scum? - Sit down!

333
00:19:44,270 --> 00:19:44,940
Sit down.

334
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:45,700
I'll handle this.

335
00:19:52,310 --> 00:19:53,770
The man who hit them is in there, right?

336
00:19:54,180 --> 00:19:55,980
I saw your cab parked outside.

337
00:19:56,270 --> 00:19:56,860
Ma'am...

338
00:19:56,880 --> 00:19:58,090
What exactly are you trying to do?

339
00:19:58,110 --> 00:19:59,530
I don't understand why you keep protecting

340
00:19:59,550 --> 00:20:00,330
this driver.

341
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:03,440
[Yang Zhao]

342
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:04,140
Mingsheng.

343
00:20:04,790 --> 00:20:05,940
She signed the settlement agreement.

344
00:20:06,550 --> 00:20:08,460
I've never met a woman this stubborn.

345
00:20:10,590 --> 00:20:11,290
Mingsheng, I don't get it.

346
00:20:11,310 --> 00:20:13,090
Why did you offer her money in the first place?

347
00:20:13,200 --> 00:20:14,660
All right, give it a rest.

348
00:20:15,270 --> 00:20:16,570
She didn't even ask for his number.

349
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:18,530
I don't think she was after money.

350
00:20:21,400 --> 00:20:22,490
I'll pay.

351
00:20:23,510 --> 00:20:24,810
But don't give her my number.

352
00:20:25,880 --> 00:20:27,050
I'll take you home first.

353
00:20:29,550 --> 00:20:30,730
Who told you to come?

354
00:20:31,400 --> 00:20:32,290
You got into trouble.

355
00:20:32,310 --> 00:20:34,010
Of course the police called your family.

356
00:20:36,030 --> 00:20:36,860
Family?

357
00:20:39,240 --> 00:20:40,140
Let me take you to the hospital first.

358
00:20:41,030 --> 00:20:41,620
No.

359
00:20:43,830 --> 00:20:45,250
If you're driving me anywhere, take me back to school.

360
00:20:48,830 --> 00:20:50,900
How can you go back to school like this?

361
00:20:51,640 --> 00:20:53,420
Fighting an 80-year-old woman over a cab?

362
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:54,380
You guys are unbelievable.

363
00:20:54,400 --> 00:20:55,460
I didn't fight her for it.

364
00:20:56,270 --> 00:20:58,180
That driver looked down on us first!

365
00:20:58,200 --> 00:20:59,010
With the way you acted,

366
00:20:59,030 --> 00:21:00,320
it's hard for anyone to respect you.

367
00:21:00,320 --> 00:21:01,650
He looked down on us from the start!

368
00:21:03,660 --> 00:21:05,140
You didn't see the way he looked at us.

369
00:21:05,550 --> 00:21:06,680
Like we were trash!

370
00:21:09,350 --> 00:21:10,370
Do you have any money left?

371
00:21:10,960 --> 00:21:11,730
What's that supposed to mean?

372
00:21:13,200 --> 00:21:14,050
Are you going to throw me some charity?

373
00:21:15,920 --> 00:21:17,010
If Mom and Dad hadn't suddenly died,

374
00:21:17,030 --> 00:21:18,460
would you have even bothered coming back?

375
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,180
All these years,

376
00:21:28,350 --> 00:21:30,010
you've never considered this place your home.

377
00:21:31,240 --> 00:21:32,660
Or any of us your family.

378
00:21:43,110 --> 00:21:44,770
I know you're still struggling to accept it.

379
00:21:46,030 --> 00:21:47,050
But no matter what,

380
00:21:47,070 --> 00:21:48,050
I'm your sister.

381
00:21:49,640 --> 00:21:51,140
Like it or not, I'm responsible for you.

382
00:21:53,920 --> 00:21:55,140
Until you finish your college entrance exams,

383
00:21:55,440 --> 00:21:56,420
I'm staying right here.

384
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:58,530
I don't need you.

385
00:21:59,680 --> 00:22:01,530
You didn't even see Mom and Dad before they died.

386
00:22:02,720 --> 00:22:04,770
I have no family left in this world.

387
00:22:05,720 --> 00:22:06,620
And I don't have a sister.

388
00:22:28,790 --> 00:22:30,330
Not bad, Deng!

389
00:22:30,350 --> 00:22:32,090
Business is booming at your boxing gym.

390
00:22:32,550 --> 00:22:33,860
With you guys coming by every day,

391
00:22:33,880 --> 00:22:34,940
how could business not be booming?

392
00:22:35,350 --> 00:22:35,900
Alright, alright.

393
00:22:36,480 --> 00:22:37,010
Have a drink.

394
00:22:37,640 --> 00:22:38,140
Take a break from training.

395
00:22:38,590 --> 00:22:39,330
Put that on the bench for me. Thanks.

396
00:22:39,350 --> 00:22:41,380
But don't just focus on making money.

397
00:22:41,590 --> 00:22:42,700
You should help Mingsheng out more.

398
00:22:42,720 --> 00:22:44,810
You really going to let him drive a cab all day to make a living?

399
00:22:46,160 --> 00:22:47,530
Deng's already helped me plenty.

400
00:22:48,640 --> 00:22:50,010
My taxi operating permit?

401
00:22:50,350 --> 00:22:51,620
Deng got that for me.

402
00:22:52,590 --> 00:22:53,860
My boss even asked about you today.

403
00:22:54,160 --> 00:22:56,010
Wanted to know if we'd done enough to help you out.

404
00:22:57,350 --> 00:22:58,010
Mingsheng,

405
00:22:58,750 --> 00:23:01,010
I don't think you need to be driving a cab either.

406
00:23:01,310 --> 00:23:01,700
How about this?

407
00:23:02,590 --> 00:23:04,420
Come manage my boxing gym.

408
00:23:04,510 --> 00:23:05,940
We'll split the profits fifty-fifty.

409
00:23:05,960 --> 00:23:06,700
It'll take some work off my hands, too.

410
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:07,490
What do you say?

411
00:23:07,640 --> 00:23:08,380
Sounds good to me.

412
00:23:08,400 --> 00:23:09,180
I'm all for it!

413
00:23:09,480 --> 00:23:11,220
But I like driving a cab.

414
00:23:12,510 --> 00:23:13,420
Being out on the road

415
00:23:14,590 --> 00:23:15,220
makes me feel free.

416
00:23:15,830 --> 00:23:16,460
And at peace.

417
00:23:16,960 --> 00:23:18,940
See? You can't put a price on doing what you love.

418
00:23:20,790 --> 00:23:21,460
Song, you're here.

419
00:23:21,480 --> 00:23:21,860
Yeah.

420
00:23:25,720 --> 00:23:26,420
Here's that woman's

421
00:23:26,850 --> 00:23:27,900
address.

422
00:23:33,270 --> 00:23:34,730
What kind of job did you do?

423
00:23:34,960 --> 00:23:36,420
She squeezed five thousand out of Mingsheng.

424
00:23:36,440 --> 00:23:37,330
I could let that slide.

425
00:23:37,510 --> 00:23:38,980
But now he has to deliver it himself?

426
00:23:39,310 --> 00:23:39,860
When is this going to end?

427
00:23:39,880 --> 00:23:41,380
Easy for you to say.

428
00:23:41,400 --> 00:23:41,980
You... you...

429
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:42,770
You make it sound so simple.

430
00:23:42,790 --> 00:23:43,940
I'm just a low-ranking cop.

431
00:23:44,070 --> 00:23:44,980
You think my job's easy?

432
00:23:45,550 --> 00:23:47,530
I can't just arrest her over this!

433
00:23:48,700 --> 00:23:53,060
[Yang Zhao]

434
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:09,010
Thanks.

435
00:24:09,010 --> 00:24:16,260
[TAXI]

436
00:25:26,270 --> 00:25:27,810
Huaken Gold Tower, please.

437
00:25:31,700 --> 00:25:32,440
[TAXI]

438
00:25:32,440 --> 00:25:32,980
Sorry.

439
00:25:33,110 --> 00:25:34,180
I'm soaking wet.

440
00:25:34,440 --> 00:25:35,900
I'll give you a little extra when we arrive.

441
00:25:55,160 --> 00:25:55,810
What happened?

442
00:25:57,500 --> 00:26:02,700
[TAXI]

443
00:26:13,030 --> 00:26:13,980
Sorry.

444
00:26:14,550 --> 00:26:15,330
The cab broke down.

445
00:26:16,400 --> 00:26:18,090
Water must've gotten into the engine.

446
00:26:19,070 --> 00:26:20,770
You'll have to get out and call another cab.

447
00:26:27,260 --> 00:26:28,160
[Chen Mingsheng]

448
00:26:28,160 --> 00:26:29,220
Chen Mingsheng.

449
00:26:33,450 --> 00:26:34,820
That was you at the station yesterday, right?

450
00:26:41,400 --> 00:26:42,290
Before I got in,

451
00:26:42,310 --> 00:26:43,700
You knew it was me, didn't you?

452
00:26:47,160 --> 00:26:47,730
No.

453
00:26:49,070 --> 00:26:49,700
It was a coincidence.

454
00:26:50,110 --> 00:26:51,050
At the police station,

455
00:26:51,270 --> 00:26:52,530
you knew I was there,

456
00:26:52,550 --> 00:26:53,420
but you wouldn't come out.

457
00:26:53,750 --> 00:26:54,810
Was that a coincidence, too?

458
00:26:58,480 --> 00:26:59,380
It's pouring.

459
00:27:00,070 --> 00:27:01,330
The car's going to flood at this rate.

460
00:27:01,350 --> 00:27:02,660
Let's get out and try pushing it.

461
00:27:03,720 --> 00:27:04,290
No need.

462
00:27:05,400 --> 00:27:07,140
We're close to Huaken Gold Tower.

463
00:27:08,270 --> 00:27:09,290
Just walk from here.

464
00:27:09,310 --> 00:27:10,570
I can help you push.

465
00:27:10,960 --> 00:27:11,730
I can manage.

466
00:27:17,310 --> 00:27:18,940
Why have you been avoiding me, Jiang Ming?

467
00:27:21,000 --> 00:27:22,490
Do you really not want to see me?

468
00:27:29,440 --> 00:27:30,330
I don't.

469
00:27:51,540 --> 00:27:52,660
[Public Security Mediation Agreement]

470
00:27:59,100 --> 00:28:01,820
[TAXI]

471
00:28:15,460 --> 00:28:18,620
♪Time passes so quickly♪

472
00:28:21,220 --> 00:28:24,340
♪I never became someone you could lean on♪

473
00:28:26,620 --> 00:28:29,340
♪There were things I never got to say♪

474
00:28:30,260 --> 00:28:33,860
♪But time has erased them for me♪

475
00:28:37,340 --> 00:28:40,100
♪People come and go, each doing their best♪

476
00:28:40,820 --> 00:28:43,700
♪Busy living their own lives♪

477
00:28:43,940 --> 00:28:47,100
♪I've learned to stop asking why...♪

478
00:28:47,120 --> 00:28:48,450
Go back before you catch a cold.

479
00:28:49,440 --> 00:28:50,140
Hurry up and push!

480
00:28:54,220 --> 00:28:56,260
♪Only later did I realize♪

481
00:28:57,780 --> 00:28:59,940
♪The hardest part♪

482
00:29:01,380 --> 00:29:03,140
♪Wasn't saying goodbye♪

483
00:29:03,700 --> 00:29:06,780
♪But knowing we'd both be okay♪

484
00:29:08,580 --> 00:29:10,260
♪Only later did I realize♪

485
00:29:10,500 --> 00:29:12,220
♪That love, in the end♪

486
00:29:12,420 --> 00:29:14,820
♪Isn't about holding on♪

487
00:29:14,980 --> 00:29:17,660
♪It's keeping someone in your heart♪

488
00:29:17,940 --> 00:29:22,580
♪As you go on with your life♪

489
00:29:29,980 --> 00:29:35,420
♪Keeping you in my heart...♪

490
00:29:35,440 --> 00:29:36,770
Could you pull the handbrake for me?

491
00:29:37,060 --> 00:29:40,700
♪As you go on with your life♪

492
00:29:44,340 --> 00:29:47,740
♪Keeping you in my heart♪

493
00:29:49,720 --> 00:29:50,940
You're soaked to the bone.

494
00:29:51,510 --> 00:29:52,660
My place is just up ahead.

495
00:29:53,200 --> 00:29:54,570
Come inside and get out of the rain.

496
00:29:56,630 --> 00:29:57,290
No.

497
00:29:58,160 --> 00:29:58,770
Thank you.

498
00:30:01,550 --> 00:30:02,460
You should get going.

499
00:30:03,270 --> 00:30:04,420
I'll take care of the rest.

500
00:30:05,030 --> 00:30:06,140
How are you going to do that?

501
00:30:08,750 --> 00:30:10,230
What are you so afraid of?

502
00:30:19,720 --> 00:30:21,000
I'm not asking you.

503
00:31:30,310 --> 00:31:31,180
Come in.

504
00:31:31,680 --> 00:31:32,490
Close the door.

505
00:31:33,620 --> 00:31:34,620
Give me my car keys.

506
00:31:59,590 --> 00:32:00,700
What's your real name?

507
00:32:01,160 --> 00:32:01,980
Jiang Ming?

508
00:32:04,880 --> 00:32:06,090
Or Chen Mingsheng?

509
00:32:09,070 --> 00:32:10,570
My name is Chen Mingsheng.

510
00:32:12,310 --> 00:32:13,330
Chen Mingsheng.

511
00:32:15,510 --> 00:32:16,700
It's me.

512
00:32:18,160 --> 00:32:19,420
I'm Yang Zhao.

513
00:32:31,070 --> 00:32:32,140
Where are you going?

514
00:32:40,880 --> 00:32:42,660
To get you some dry clothes.

515
00:32:57,640 --> 00:32:58,140
Yang Zhao.

516
00:32:59,550 --> 00:33:00,140
Yang Zhao.

517
00:33:06,340 --> 00:33:10,220
[Tianrong Pharmacy]

518
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:16,820
Hello.

519
00:33:17,160 --> 00:33:18,420
What can I get you?

520
00:33:19,680 --> 00:33:21,180
She got soaked in the rain. Now she has a fever.

521
00:33:51,200 --> 00:33:51,820
Yang Zhao.

522
00:33:55,920 --> 00:33:56,530
Yang Zhao.

523
00:34:07,440 --> 00:34:08,320
Come on, sit up.

524
00:34:26,590 --> 00:34:27,260
Drink a little more.

525
00:37:27,550 --> 00:37:28,340
Five.

526
00:37:29,240 --> 00:37:30,220
What can I get you?

527
00:37:30,240 --> 00:37:31,740
Two orders of steamed buns and two bowls of porridge.

528
00:37:32,240 --> 00:37:32,700
Sure.

529
00:37:38,920 --> 00:37:39,740
You're awake.

530
00:37:40,530 --> 00:37:41,520
I got breakfast.

531
00:37:43,630 --> 00:37:44,340
Ms. Yang.

532
00:37:45,630 --> 00:37:46,340
I'm sorry.

533
00:37:47,630 --> 00:37:48,970
Sorry for troubling you last night.

534
00:37:51,880 --> 00:37:53,010
Are you leaving already?

535
00:37:54,630 --> 00:37:55,940
Is your leg okay?

536
00:37:58,320 --> 00:37:59,450
That's not what I meant.

537
00:38:00,630 --> 00:38:02,010
You got soaked last night, too.

538
00:38:03,030 --> 00:38:03,860
Your leg...

539
00:38:04,190 --> 00:38:05,650
Shouldn't you get it checked at the hospital?

540
00:38:06,670 --> 00:38:07,380
No need.

541
00:38:08,760 --> 00:38:10,740
I'll pay you back.

542
00:38:12,400 --> 00:38:13,220
Chen Mingsheng.

543
00:38:15,510 --> 00:38:16,820
Will you come see me again?

544
00:38:17,940 --> 00:38:19,340
♪I remember how my fingertips♪

545
00:38:19,580 --> 00:38:22,340
♪Once lingered on your face♪

546
00:38:24,020 --> 00:38:25,220
♪It feels so far away♪

547
00:38:25,500 --> 00:38:26,700
♪Yet my memories of you♪

548
00:38:26,940 --> 00:38:29,460
♪Seem frozen in the past♪

549
00:38:30,980 --> 00:38:32,820
♪We never said goodbye♪

550
00:38:33,060 --> 00:38:34,740
♪We parted without a word in the end♪

551
00:38:34,980 --> 00:38:38,780
♪Silently, we drifted apart♪

552
00:38:39,100 --> 00:38:40,340
♪I don't blame you♪

553
00:38:40,580 --> 00:38:41,980
♪I'll tell myself I once had♪

554
00:38:42,060 --> 00:38:45,460
♪I'll tell myself I once had you♪

555
00:38:47,820 --> 00:38:49,660
♪I wanted us to share♪

556
00:38:49,740 --> 00:38:52,020
♪A simple life without regrets♪

557
00:38:54,140 --> 00:38:55,460
♪And I almost told you♪

558
00:38:55,820 --> 00:38:56,900
♪What that rush of tears♪

559
00:38:57,020 --> 00:39:00,340
♪Had moved me to promise♪

560
00:39:01,300 --> 00:39:02,980
♪It's a shame that you and I♪

561
00:39:03,100 --> 00:39:04,620
♪Were bound to face a rough road♪

562
00:39:04,820 --> 00:39:07,140
♪Bound to go nowhere♪

563
00:39:07,700 --> 00:39:09,940
♪I won't be sad♪

564
00:39:10,700 --> 00:39:12,060
♪I'll tell myself I once had♪

565
00:39:12,220 --> 00:39:15,820
